<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  TC8 §4.8.6.2 TCP_CHECKSUM_04: TCP MUST use clock-driven selection of
  initial sequence numbers — the ISN MUST change across consecutive
  active OPENs. Derived from RFC 1122 §4.2.2.9 p87 ISN Selection
  (MUST), RFC 793 §3.3 p27 Sequence Numbers.

  Despite the §4.8.6.2 "Checksum" section heading, this case asserts
  ISN distinctness, not checksum correctness. The placement is a TC8
  v3.0 spec quirk; the substantive RFC mapping is RFC 1122 §4.2.2.9.

  v3.0 Test Procedure (p301-p320.txt:216):
    1. TESTER: Cause DUT-side application to issue CONNECT (cycle 1).
    2. DUT:    Send SYN.
    3. TESTER: Send RST,ACK to take DUT to CLOSED state.
    4. TESTER: Cause DUT-side CONNECT again (cycle 2).
    5. DUT:    Send SYN.
    6. TESTER: Verify SYN2.seq != SYN1.seq.

  Mechanism (verdict computed from captured ISN snapshots):
    The DUT is driven through two consecutive active OPENs on the
    SAME 4-tuple. Cycle 1's SYN is aborted by a RST+ACK against an
    unbound destination port (RST+ACK ack=ISN_d+1, an acceptable RST
    for a SYN-SENT socket per RFC 793 §3.9 — this IS spec step 3).
    The DUT-side socket then closes, the local port is released, and
    cycle 2 reuses the same local port for the second active OPEN.

    Each cycle's SYN seq is captured directly off the wire into
    `captured.cycle1_isn` / `captured.cycle2_isn` with the matching
    `*_captured` sentinel bools. The verdict falls out of these
    captured fields alone, so any SYN frames replayed through the
    main observation pipeline after the captures complete never
    disturb the SCXML's evaluation.

    An earlier wire-driven SCXML guard ("transition on tcp_observed
    SYN with `prior_isn != 0 ∧ seq != prior_isn`") raced against the
    stimulus-first lifecycle: the cycle-1 SYN is buffered and the
    prior-ISN reference is already populated by the time SCXML begins
    consuming events, so `seq == prior_isn` fires `fail_isn_unchanged`
    on the cycle-1 SYN itself. Evaluating the two captured ISN
    snapshots (this file) sidesteps that race entirely.

  Verdict ladder (first-match wins per W3C SCXML RFC 793 §3.13, fail-first):
    1. `cycle1_isn_captured == false` → `fail_no_cycle1_isn`
       (snippet timed out before SYN1 hit the wire — likely UT RPC
       failure or a negative-flip path where dut_iface_ip is
       mis-pointed).
    2. `cycle2_isn_captured == false` → `fail_no_cycle2_isn`
       (cycle 2's snippet timed out — same diagnostic).
    3. `cycle1_isn == cycle2_isn` → `fail_isn_unchanged`
       (RFC 1122 §4.2.2.9 violation — DUT reused the prior ISN).
    4. fall-through → `pass`.

  Negative flip: ipv4.dut_iface_ip=10.99.99.99 makes the SYN capture
  filter (`src host <dut_iface_ip>`) unreachable on every observed
  SYN; both captures time out and the verdict lands on
  `fail_no_cycle1_isn`. (The earliest-fail-first ordering means
  cycle 2's matching failure is masked by cycle 1's, which is fine
  — the failure surface is uniformly "no DUT SYN observable from
  this case's vantage".)

  ## Port-quad selection — kBasicsActiveLocalPort + 180 / +180

  +180 sits clear of the §4.8 active-OPEN cluster (FLAGS_INVALID_03..06
  at +20..+25, BASICS_17 at +120, ACK_02/04 at +130/+131,
  NAGLE_02/03 at +132/+133, OUT_OF_ORDER + PROBING_WINDOWS +
  RETRANSMISSION_TO at +143..+156, CONNECTION_ESTAB_03 at +176..+178)
  per the active-open port-quad collision rules
  (reference_active_open_port_quad_collision.md).
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       xmlns:cpp="urn:sce:cpp"
       version="1.0"
       name="tcp_checksum_04"
       datamodel="null"
       initial="evaluate_isn_observations">

  <sce:context id="captured"
               cpp:type="tc8::TcpCaptured"
               cpp:include="sce_integration/tcp_captured.h"/>

  <sce:context id="expected"
               cpp:type="tc8::Ipv4Expected"
               cpp:include="sce_integration/ipv4_expected.h"/>

  <state id="evaluate_isn_observations">
    <onentry>
      <send event="evaluate" delay="0ms"/>
    </onentry>
    <transition event="evaluate"
                cond="cpp:not captured.cycle1_isn_captured"
                target="fail_no_cycle1_isn"/>
    <transition event="evaluate"
                cond="cpp:not captured.cycle2_isn_captured"
                target="fail_no_cycle2_isn"/>
    <transition event="evaluate"
                cond="cpp:captured.cycle1_isn == captured.cycle2_isn"
                target="fail_isn_unchanged"/>
    <transition event="evaluate" target="pass"/>
  </state>

  <final id="pass">
    <donedata>
      <content>{"verdict":"pass"}</content>
    </donedata>
  </final>

  <final id="fail_no_cycle1_isn">
    <donedata>
      <content>{"verdict":"fail","reason":"cycle1_syn_capture_timeout"}</content>
    </donedata>
  </final>

  <final id="fail_no_cycle2_isn">
    <donedata>
      <content>{"verdict":"fail","reason":"cycle2_syn_capture_timeout"}</content>
    </donedata>
  </final>

  <final id="fail_isn_unchanged">
    <donedata>
      <content>{"verdict":"fail","reason":"dut_reused_prior_isn_across_active_opens"}</content>
    </donedata>
  </final>
</scxml>
